      "id": "3946cb4bf36a"
    },
    {
      "question": "Are StorageEnv seeds independent samples?",
      "answer": "No. StorageEnv derives cycle worlds from seed plus cycle, so adjacent seeds are shifted windows of one another; treat across-seed spreads as smoother than independent draws.",
      "kind": "explicit",
      "sources": [
        "noisy-suite-review"
      ],
      "energy": 0.8479921447227143,
      "born_cycle": 0,
      "recorded_ts": "2026-08-20T00:02:31+00:00",
      "last_used_cycle": 4,
      "uses": 1,
      "lineage": [],
      "id": "067b8223d3d7"
    },
    {
      "question": "Can multiple workflow jobs settle the memory store in parallel?",
      "answer": "No. The store is a single JSON file with no locking, so one settler at a time: settle from a serialized queue or a workflow concurrency group, never from parallel jobs.",
      "kind": "explicit",
      "sources": [
        "docs/integrations/ci-lesson-store"
      ],
      "energy": 1.2999999998768572,
      "born_cycle": 0,
      "recorded_ts": "2026-08-20T00:02:31+00:00",
      "last_used_cycle": 3,
      "uses": 1,
      "lineage": [],
      "id": "6de9b640e935"
    },
    {
      "question": "Does a merged PR that carries no ticket cost the store anything?",
      "answer": "Yes, and it used to be free to forget: a tick charges every living entry upkeep, so ticking per merge rather than per settlement bills memory for time it was never consulted in. Credit is capped at max_energy, so bounded credit means bounded runway; drive the clock from evidence, and watch ticking_without_evidence.",
      "kind": "explicit",
